==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Shy Boy]] (100%) spawns.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 20~33.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 20~33.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Squire Rel]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Shy Boy]] (400%) spawns.
**1 [[Shy Boy]] (400%) spawns.

==Strategy==
[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] is exceptional here in stalling the 1st Shy Boy, so use this time to upgrade your wallet. At higher levels, only a couple are needed to kill it, due to its low magnification. The money garnered from the Shy Boy is more than enough to get your attackers on the field, and a low cost one like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] is very helpful. [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] can also help chip the other two Shy Boys. Once those Shy Boys are down, this is an effortless cleanup.

On {{4c}}, overwhelm the enemies with Cyborg Cats and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]]. Deploy an [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to assist them in taking down the two Shy Boys that come out after a while. Since the Doge Darks are buffed, you want many meatshields to ensure they can't break through by helping the Shy Boys.

